<Layout title="About – FutureMedia" fonts="display">
<main class="about">
<section class="about-story">
<p class="eyebrow">Future Media</p>
<h1>Where it began</h1>
<p>When Future Media was established in 2019, we inherited something rare, a portfolio of broadcast brands that Namibians had already spent decades trusting. Omulunga Radio, Radiowave, 99FM, Fresh FM, Nova 103.5, OneAfrica.tv, and Property News weren't new ideas. They were household names, woven into the daily rhythms of Namibian life. Together, we already reached more than two million Namibians, over 70% of the country, across every major language, demographic, and region.</p>
<p>The question facing us wasn't how to build an audience. We already had one. The question was what to do with that reach, and what responsibility it carried to our audience and our clients.</p>
<ul class="about-stats">
<li><b>2019</b><span>Established</span></li>
<li><b>2M+</b><span>Namibians reached</span></li>
<li><b>70%</b><span>Of the country</span></li>
<li><b>20</b><span>Trusted brands</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section class="about-story">
<h2>The evolution</h2>
<p>What followed was not a dramatic reinvention. It was something more deliberate, a gradual, considered expansion, led by a management team that understood Namibia from the inside. Our broadcasting roots stayed intact. But around them, new capabilities grew.</p>
<p>Today, we are Namibia's largest independent media group, an ecosystem of 20 trusted brands across radio, television, digital, branding, property, and retail media, with over 475 active client partnerships, many spanning a decade or more, and an average of more than 27 million audience engagements over any three-month period.</p>
<p class="about-line">We grow businesses and support communities through meaningful connections. That has always been what this was about. Everything else, the platforms, the technology, the new capabilities, is in service of that.</p>
<ul class="about-stats">
<li><b>475+</b><span>Client partnerships</span></li>
<li><b>27M</b><span>Engagements each quarter</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
